[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Identity kind [39m[49m

[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mWhat kind of identifier is userId — an authenticated identity, or a client-side tracking id?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mServer-issued, post-auth[39m
     [38;5;246mThe login API returns the real user id after authenticating. Authoritative, but only exists after a successful [39m
     [38;5;246mlogin — so it can't be a login() input; it'd be login() output that everything downstream consumes.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Client-generated tracking id
     [38;5;246mAn anonymous id minted in the browser (e.g. UUID in localStorage) that survives across sessions and attaches to [39m
     [38;5;246mevents whether or not anyone is logged in. This one genuinely can be a login() parameter.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Both, separate concerns
     [38;5;246mA persistent anonymous device/visitor id, plus the authenticated user id once login succeeds, correlated together.
[39m     [38;5;246mMost capable, most machinery.[39m
